// Device safeguards (measured, docs/WALL-PRO-EFFECTS.md): the ice is a 3D ray-march. On a GPU one draw costs ~0.2 ms of the page's main thread (RTX 3060); with
// software rendering (no GPU) it costs 400-550 ms and the whole page falls to 1-3 fps. So: a software renderer never draws Living Ice; a device whose draws keep
// taking over SLOW_DRAW_MS gives up after SLOW_DRAWS of them; both show the readable static fallback, exactly as a device without WebGL2 does.
const SOFTWARE_RENDERER = /swiftshader|llvmpipe|softpipe|software|basic render/i;
const SLOW_DRAW_MS = 100, SLOW_DRAWS = 3;
let slowDraws = 0;

